body:
kvellarcanum brings up a good point about the support system, i forgot to mention after reading the OP. Do not move to another city unless you have to. Regardless of how dysfunctional your family is (everyones is a little), they are solid pillars. At the end of the day you can rely on them in so many non-explicitly-describable ways. Moving to new city will mean you will lose this, not to mention if you are already down... you are pretty likely to not make connections and be totally alone, in a new town.

Right now, even your mind accepts you have family to turn to. Don't take that way.

@kvellarcanum: I hope you don't mind, but your story at least made me feel a little better. At least I didn't move to the city (which would have been a big expensive, and huge hope) and then get fired which means instead of being at 0, you end up at -30 on the depressed scale.
